.TH MAPS-STORAGE-INSPECTOR 1 "September 2026" "MapsMessaging" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
maps-storage-inspector \- inspect and export MAPS dynamic storage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B maps-storage-inspector
.B --input
.I path
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B maps-storage-inspector
performs read-only offline inspection of MAPS dynamic storage partition stores.
It can validate storage structure, decode stored messages using compatible MAPS
server libraries, and export active events as NDJSON.
.PP
Use a stopped-server copy or filesystem snapshot when investigating possible
corruption. The inspector does not intentionally modify the input store.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --input " path"
Storage snapshot, destination, store, or partition input path.
.TP
.B --decode
Decode selected messages without writing an event export.
.TP
.BI --output " file"
Write decoded active events as NDJSON.
.TP
.BI --report " file"
Write inspection findings and summary records as NDJSON.
.TP
.BI --destination " name"
Select a destination by its exact resource name.
.TP
.BI --start-event-id " id"
Select events starting at the inclusive event identifier.
.TP
.BI --end-event-id " id"
Select events ending at the inclusive event identifier.
.TP
.BI --threads " count"
Set inspection worker count. The default is 4.
.TP
.BI --max-record-bytes " bytes"
Set the maximum storage record size accepted during inspection.
.TP
.BI --max-archive-bytes " bytes"
Set the maximum expanded compressed-partition size.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates completed checks, 1 corruption or read failure, 2 usage/runtime/output
failure, and 3 warnings or incomplete coverage.
.SH FILES
The tool reads MAPS dynamic storage snapshots and may create NDJSON report and
event export files specified by the operator.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR maps-ndjson-viewer (1),
.BR maps-apps (7)
.SH DOCUMENTATION
See storage_inspector/docs/storage-inspector.md in the maps_apps source tree and
storage_inspector/README.md for detailed storage-format and operational guidance.
